            <br />
            <span class="auto-style5">1) <strong>What is vaccination?<br />
            </strong></span><span class="auto-style6">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Child vaccination is the process of giving vaccines to children to protect them from various infectious diseases. Vaccines help the child’s immune system develop protection against harmful viruses and bacteria without actually causing the illness. This process is essential for building immunity during the early years when children are most vulnerable to serious diseases like measles, polio, diphtheria, hepatitis B, and tuberculosis. Vaccination not only protects the individual child but also helps prevent the spread of diseases in the community through herd immunity. In most countries, including India, a schedule is followed under national health programs to ensure timely and complete vaccination. These vaccines are thoroughly tested and approved by health authorities and are proven to be safe and effective. Regular child vaccination is a crucial step toward ensuring a healthy future for children and society as a whole.<br />
            </span></td>
    </tr>
